## Description

This detection identifies the execution of **Certutil (certutil.exe)** using **Microsoft Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Creation)**.

Certutil is a legitimate Microsoft command-line utility used to manage certificates and certificate services. However, because it is installed by default on Windows systems, threat actors frequently abuse it as a **Living-off-the-Land Binary (LOLBin)** to download malicious payloads, encode or decode files, and evade application control policies.

Monitoring Certutil execution helps defenders identify suspicious activity associated with malware delivery and post-exploitation.

