# Analyst Notes

Certutil is one of the most frequently abused Windows LOLBins because it is digitally signed by Microsoft and available by default on most Windows systems. Adversaries commonly use it to download payloads, transfer files, encode or decode malicious content, and bypass application control mechanisms.

This detection provides valuable visibility into suspicious Certutil activity and should be correlated with file creation events, PowerShell execution, registry modifications, scheduled task creation, and network connections to identify potential malware delivery or post-exploitation behavior.

